    "lawCode": "Amd §2590-h, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6355\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to permitting\nmembership in certain school related associations by grandparents of\ncertain children\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill will allow grandparents who have the written permission of\ntheir grandchild's parent or legal guardian to participate in the\nchild's school parent's association or parent-teacher association\nwithin a community school district in the City of New York.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSubdivision 15 of Section of 2590-h of the education law is amended by\nadding a new closing paragraph to read as follows: the chancellor\nshall by rule or regulation provide for the involvement including\nmembership, in any parent's association or parent-teacher association\nestablished pursuant to this subdivision, of a grandparent of a child\nwho attends a school within the jurisdiction of the community school\ndistrict, where the parent or other person having legal custody of\nsuch child has indicated in writing that such grandparent provides\ndirect care and exercises control over the child on a regular basis.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nAlthough they are not always designated as legal guardians,\ngrandparents often take a very active role in the lives of their\ngrandchildren, including having custodial care and direct control over\nthe day-to-day life of their grandchildren. Thus, these grandparents\noften wish to become involved with the parent, or parent-teacher\nassociation at their grandchild's school. Under current law, unless\nthese grandparents are the designated legal guardians, they have not\nhad an official designation under the law allowing them to participate\nin these associations. This legislation would allow grandparents, when\ngiven written permission from the child's parent or legal guardian, to\nparticipate in parent associations, as determined by a rule or\nregulation formulated by the Chancellor of the New York City Board of\nEducation.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2003-04:  S.69/A.1649\n2005-06:  S.927/A.1714\n2007-08:  S.1309/A.2684\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided that the amendments\nto subdivision 15 of section 2590-h of the education law made by\nsection one of this act shall be subject to the expiration and\nreversion of such subdivision pursuant to section 34 of chapter 91 of\nthe laws of 2002, as amended, when upon such date the provisions of\nsection two of this act shall take effect.\n",
