    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6355A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the education law, in relation to permitting membership in\ncertain school related associations by grandparents of certain children\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill will allow grandparents who\nhave the written permission of their grandchild's parent or legal\nguardian to participate in the child's school parent's association or\nparent-teacher association within a community school district in the\nCity of New York.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSubdivision 15 of Section 2590-h of\nthe education law is amended by adding a new closing paragraph to\nread as follows: the chancellor shall by rule or regulation provide\nfor the involvement including membership, in any parent's association\nor parent-teacher association established pursuant to this\nsubdivision, of a grandparent of a child who attends a school within\nthe jurisdiction of the community school district, where the parent\nor other person having legal custody of such child has indicated in\nwriting that such grandparent provides direct care and exercises\ncontrol over the child on a regular basis.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nAlthough they are not always designated as legal\nguardians, grandparents often take a very active role in the lives of\ntheir grandchildren, including having custodial care and direct\ncontrol over the day-to-day life of their grandchildren. Thus, these\ngrandparents often wish to become involved with the parent, or\nparent-teacher association at their grandchild's school. Under\ncurrent law, unless these grandparents are the designated legal\nguardians, they have not had an official designation under the law\nallowing them to participate in these associations. This legislation\nwould allow grandparents, when given written permission from the\nchild's parent or legal guardian, to participate in parent\nassociations, as determined by a rule or regulation formulated by the\nChancellor of the New York City Board of Education.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2003-04:  S.69/A.1649\n2005-06:  S.927/A.1714\n2007-08:  S.1309/A.2684\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect\nimmediately; provided that\nthe amendments to subdivision 15 of section 2590-h of the education\nlaw made by section one of this act shall be subject to the\nexpiration and reversion of such subdivision pursuant to section 34\n\n\nof chapter 91 of the laws of 2002, as amended, when upon such date\nthe provisions of section two of this act shall take effect.\n\n",
